<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Dialectic tests a position from within</h2>
      <labels><label variant="solid">Important correction</label></labels>
      <h3>Not a mechanical thesis–antithesis–synthesis formula.</h3>
      <grid recipe="process-steps" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item colspan="20">
          <h3>Specify</h3>
          <p>State what the position actually claims, in its strongest form.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20">
          <h3>Press</h3>
          <p>Work through what it must exclude, assume, or fail to contain.</p>
          <labels><label variant="outline">Internal pressure</label></labels>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20">
          <h3>Revise</h3>
          <p>Build a richer account that incorporates the lesson rather than merely replacing the first claim.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p><b>The pressure is internal:</b> the position encounters limits as it is worked through.</p>
      <p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/hegel-dialectics/">Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “Hegel’s Dialectics”</a></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>